{
  "id": "schnakenberg-well-mixed-biology",
  "name": "Schnakenberg autocatalytic morphogen reaction core",
  "description": "Well-mixed two-species reaction core with activator autocatalysis and substrate depletion. No diffusion or spatial Turing pattern is claimed. Unlike the active Brusselator, it uses direct feed into the second species and a three-reaction autocatalytic scheme. Illustrative parameter values, initial conditions and horizon selected for this teaching example; not fitted observations. Signed net-rate flows encode equations, not material transfer claims. No clamps or hidden state resets.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0",
  "reference": "Schnakenberg (1979), Simple chemical reaction systems with limit cycle behaviour, Journal of Theoretical Biology81:389-400.",
  "category": "biology",
  "stocks": [
    {
      "id": "schnakenberg-well-mixed-biology:Activator",
